Aerie-Purpose: Key Helium's fingerprinting noise tokens and the per-site "off" switch on the site (scheme plus registrable domain) instead of the origin, so x.example.com and y.example.com show the same canvas, audio and core count, and turning protection off for one covers the other.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: content/browser/helium_noise/noise_token_data.cc (HeliumNoiseTokenData::GetTokens), chrome/browser/helium_noise/helium_noise_settings.cc (SetHeliumNoiseEnabledForOrigin, GetHeliumNoiseState), content/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
Aerie-Kind: hook

Amends helium-chromium/patches/helium/core/noise/core.patch (issue #114, part of #87). Helium
derives the tokens from SHA-256(session token || origin.Serialize()), so every origin got its own
seed, and the HELIUM_NOISE exception was set for one origin. A tracker on one site can load a
script from any number of subdomains, so the origin is the wrong unit; so is a per-origin switch.

The key function is in the overlay, components/aerie_fingerprint (site_key.h), with unit tests
(aerie_fingerprint_unittests). NoiseSiteKey(origin, partition) is net::SchemefulSite(origin) and an
optional partition string; nothing passes a partition yet, and keying on the Workspace (#121) will
pass one. NoiseSitePattern(url) gives the content-setting pattern for the same hosts (it is
ContentSettingsPattern::FromURLToSchemefulSitePattern, for http and https only), so the key and the
switch cannot disagree.

The switch is now "scheme://[*.]registrable-domain", for example "https://[*.]example.com" (the
scheme and the host itself for an IP address or a name without a registrable domain). The scheme is
part of the pattern because it is part of the key: http://example.com and https://example.com are
two sites, with two seeds and two switches. Origin-scoped "off" exceptions that an earlier build
stored are turned into site exceptions the first time the setting is read or changed
(GetHeliumNoiseState or the setter), once per profile object, and the migration is idempotent. The off-the-record profile is not migrated: its
exceptions live in memory and start empty (HELIUM_NOISE is DONT_INHERIT_IN_INCOGNITO), so a switch
set in incognito is never written to disk and never reaches the regular profile.

The new GN dependency on chrome/browser sits after //components/application_locale_storage on
purpose: adblock/0001 puts its line between that entry and the one before it, and its hunk context
must stay adjacent. The hunk of onboarding/0001 in this file moves down by one line.

